          "enhanced_information": "The development of the disease characterized by abnormal hemoglobin polymerization leading to complications like stroke, aplastic crisis, and auto-splenectomy is primarily associated with missense mutations rather than frameshift mutations. Missense mutations alter hemoglobin structure, leading to polymerization under hypoxia, acidosis, or dehydration, resulting in distorted RBC shape and hemolysis, ultimately causing the observed complications. Evidence paths support the relationship between altered hemoglobin, polymerization, and complications, aligning with the consensus that missense mutations play a key role in this genetic condition."
